{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinearIncrementingEntityIdGenerator","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This entity id generator creates linearly incrementing entity ids","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless an entity is marked as unused then the marked id is returned next in a FIFO order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an increased generation."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The slot index 0 is reserved and never provided; slots start at generation 0. A slot whose generation reaches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32.max"},{"type":"text","text":" is retired and never provided again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Furthermore it respects order of entity ids on initialization, meaning the provided ids on initialization will be provided in order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until all are in use. After that the free entities start at the lowest available id increasing linearly skipping already in-use entity ids."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityCreated","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityDestroyed","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityComponentHash","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityIdentifier","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityIde